// =============================================================================
// 02_anomaly_forecast.kql
// Label: [NET-NEW]  |  v2 intelligence layer (Detect + Predict)
//
// Replaces static CPU/spool/duration thresholds with seasonality-aware anomaly
// detection and forward forecasting -- moving the tool from "gateway went
// offline" to "this gateway will saturate in ~2 hours."
//
// All functions are native KQL, no external dependencies, [Feasible-now] in
// Fabric Eventhouse.
// Sources:
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/kusto/query/anomaly-detection?view=microsoft-fabric
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/kusto/query/time-series-analysis?view=microsoft-fabric
//
// [Unverified] Column/table names (bronze_system_counter, SystemCPUPercent,
//   CounterTimeUTC, etc.) per the project schema; confirm in Phase 5.
// =============================================================================

// ---- 1. Per-gateway CPU anomalies (seasonal, last 7 days, 5-min grain) -------
bronze_system_counter
| make-series CpuPct = avg(SystemCPUPercent) default=0
    on CounterTimeUTC from ago(7d) to now() step 5m
    by GatewayObjectId
| extend (Anomalies, AnomalyScore, Baseline) =
    series_decompose_anomalies(CpuPct, 1.5, -1, 'linefit')
| mv-expand CounterTimeUTC to typeof(datetime),
            CpuPct to typeof(double),
            Anomalies to typeof(int),
            AnomalyScore to typeof(double),
            Baseline to typeof(double)
| where Anomalies != 0 and AnomalyScore > 2.5
| project GatewayObjectId, CounterTimeUTC, CpuPct, Baseline, AnomalyScore
| order by AnomalyScore desc

// ---- 2. Spool-disk exhaustion FORECAST (trend, non-seasonal) -----------------
// Forecast free space 24 steps (2h at 5-min grain) ahead; flag if the lowest
// forecast crosses a danger floor. Feed the flagged rows to Activator.
//
// let danger_floor_gb = 10.0;
// bronze_disk_spool
// | make-series FreeGB = avg(FreeSpaceBytes)/1073741824.0 default=0
//     on CollectedAtUTC from ago(3d) to now() step 5m
//     by GatewayHostName
// | extend Forecast = series_decompose_forecast(FreeGB, 24)
// | extend MinForecastGB = series_stats_dynamic(Forecast).min
// | where MinForecastGB < danger_floor_gb
// | project GatewayHostName, MinForecastGB, Forecast

// ---- 3. Query-duration distribution drift (per data source) ------------------
// Detect when a datasource's p95 duration shifts -- early warning of a source or
// network regression before it becomes a failure.
//
// bronze_query_execution
// | make-series P95 = percentile(QueryExecutionDuration, 95) default=0
//     on QueryExecutionEndTimeUTC from ago(14d) to now() step 1h
//     by DataSource
// | extend (Anom, Score, Base) = series_decompose_anomalies(P95, 2.0, -1, 'linefit')
// | mv-expand QueryExecutionEndTimeUTC to typeof(datetime), P95 to typeof(double),
//             Anom to typeof(int), Score to typeof(double)
// | where Anom > 0
// | project DataSource, QueryExecutionEndTimeUTC, P95, Score

// ---- 4. Cluster load-skew score (fleet health) -------------------------------
// Coefficient of variation of query load across nodes in a cluster.
// High CV = one node is hot; the cluster is not balancing.
//
// bronze_query_execution
// | where QueryExecutionEndTimeUTC > ago(1h)
// | summarize NodeQueries = count() by GatewayObjectId
// | summarize LoadSkewCV = stdev(NodeQueries) / avg(NodeQueries), Nodes = count()
// | extend SkewAlert = LoadSkewCV > 0.5   // tune threshold
